    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "You know, I never try and speculate on motivations. I've worked with governors in both political parties. uh... over the last seven months and uh... i i must tell you that uh... you know our hearts go out to the people of new york literally one and five fatalities in this country we're in the state of new york and frankly that was uh... result in part of decisions that the governor made mayor of new york city made uh... they were they were slow to respond slow to act But it is encouraging to see in places all across the country that we are opening up again. I mean, it's amazing. We've literally seen more jobs added back to this economy in three months than Barack Obama and Joe Biden saw added to the economy in eight years. Now, we have a ways to go because at the top of the pandemic, we'd lost 22 million American jobs. But we're going to continue to work with states, give them the very best information that we can. New York has been low and steady for some time. We'll continue to give them the very best counsel. But we'll also continue to drive forward to open up our economy and open up our schools. Buck is a really big part. of open in this economy of you know my wife's a school teacher uh... she'll be going back to school on on uh... next wednesday as she teaches art of the elementary school in the washington area and uh... we just also recognize for the sake of our kids for the sake of working families who got open up our schools again too and we'll keep driving for that in every state including including yours",
