    "turn_text": "but it's such an important issue and i must tell you that i am uh... i'm shocked that no speaker the democrat national convention has spoken about the violence in our streets in our major cities it really is remarkable when you see portland seattle chicago new york city literally at times in flames uh... with uh... you know with violent uprisings, with violence against citizens, against law enforcement officers, and not a word other than vague references to peaceful protest has been uttered to my knowledge by any of the major speakers at the Democratic National Convention. And look, what President Trump and I are determined to do. is to stand by the men and women of law enforcement at every level to make sure that they have the resources to bring safety to our streets but also to improve public safety we're committed to that in the wake of the murder of George Floyd in Minneapolis the president signed an executive order and he said look we're going to provide new resources for law enforcement we're not going to defund the police not now not ever We're going to rather we're going to fund them for more resources, more training to improve public safety. And at the same time, we're also going to look for ways to continue to improve the lives of our African-American neighbors in our cities and all of our minority communities and all of our families that live in urban centers around the country. I mean, this president in our first three years had the lowest unemployment ever recorded for African-Americans. The highest investment in history in historically black colleges and universities senator tim scott uh... author to build a president signed to create eight thousand opportunity zones that have generated billions of investments creating jobs in our inner city for a minority of communities i mean that that choice the democrats which would offer with joe biden and others seem to suggest we got to make a choice between supporting law enforcement supporting our african-american community or their uh... our other minorities that the truth is We have done both will continue to do both. And I believe as this president stands with law enforcement and stands for for public safety and law and order for every American regardless of race or credit or color that we're going to win four more years for President Donald Trump in the White House.",
